    "done_when": "On the conductor-current fixture, measured and committed: (1) the reverse-mode derivative, the forward-mode JVP, and central finite differences at three steps for the same scalar functional, so reverse-versus-forward agreement is known; (2) the implicit-function-theorem derivative at the converged fixed point computed explicitly, solving (I - dG/dpsi) x = dG/dtheta v at the terminal state with the map G the route iterates, compared with all three; (3) the derivative rule the Picard route actually uses, read from nova/equilibrium/fixed_point.py and forward.py (custom vjp, unrolled differentiation of the loop, or a stop_gradient on part of the state such as the topology partition, a normalisation scalar or the support), named with file and line; (4) the term responsible, isolated by replacing one ingredient at a time (for example differentiating with the partition or normalisation treated as live rather than stopped) until reverse matches the implicit-function derivative and finite differences, each replacement measured. Also check whether the moment-map ladder failure shares the cause. Measurement only: change no solver source; a benchmark script under benchmarks/ is yours. Run CPU work in place with JAX_PLATFORMS=cpu; for H200 work the coordinator authorises RECKON_ALLOW_NESTED_LAUNCH=1 scripts/nova_lane/run.sh (H200 rung, betelgeuse gpu_0003_grpA, one card, explicit --mem, JAX_PLATFORMS=cuda, shared interpreter, no uv on the compute node); the general srun/sbatch/salloc fence does not forbid that path. The worktree registry is read-only in your fence: for another revision use git archive into /tmp, never git worktree. While a SLURM job runs write status: blocked with a valid wait_probe and wait_terminal COMPLETED. Write findings into docs/evidence/fragments/forward-solver-route-integrity/fsri-picard-derivative-contract-rca.html with a data-ink figure of derivative estimate against step for each method. Every uv command carries --no-sync and nothing runs uv sync. The manifest status is one of complete, blocked or failed.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
